# Tax and pricing strategy notes. NOT committed, and the repo being PUBLIC is
# the whole reason: the document works through how to present a bundled
# transaction so the advertising half is not swept into the taxable half, and
# it reasons about list prices against a discount ladder.
#
# Publishing that would be self-defeating twice over. The analysis itself warns
# that contract and website language are substantial evidence of how a sale
# should be taxed -- so a public note about how to frame the split is evidence
# against the split. And the discount ladder is the negotiating position; a
# distributor who can read it already knows the floor.
circuits-ai-payments-addendum.md

# Roundcube plugin configs. The .dist templates ARE committed; the real files
# never are, because they hold shared secrets — CALENDAR_API_SECRET today, and
# ccsignature's upload settings next.
#
# cccalendar's config.inc.php.dist has told people since it was written that
# this file "is gitignored by the repo's rule". Until now that was simply not
# true: `git check-ignore` exited 1. Nothing had leaked, because no real config
# had been created yet — the trap was armed and had not been stepped on.
mail/roundcube-plugins/*/config.inc.php
